# Ask before commit or push

Do not run `git commit`, `git push`, or open a pull request at the end of other work.

When the work is ready, stop and ask. Commit, push, or open a pull request only after an explicit approval in that same conversation. Approval sounds like "commit this", "push it", or "open the PR". Finishing the task is not approval.

"Commit and push" and "open the PR" are approval for that request. Do not wait for a second confirmation.
